Package: bootlace
Title: Bootstrap Inference and Plots for Logistic, Emax and Cox Models
Version: 0.1.0
Authors@R: person("Justin", "Wilkins", email = "justin.wilkins@occams.com",
    role = c("aut", "cre", "cph"))
Description: Case-resampling bootstrap inference for fitted binomial
    generalized linear models (GLMs), logistic maximum-effect (Emax)
    exposure-response models and Cox proportional hazards models. Returns
    percentile confidence intervals, plus bias-corrected and accelerated
    (BCa) and profile-likelihood intervals for Emax models (Efron and
    Tibshirani (1993, ISBN:978-0412042317)), and warns when the number of
    events per variable is too low for the model (Peduzzi et al. (1996)
    <doi:10.1016/S0895-4356(96)00236-3>). Companion functions plot
    response curves with bootstrap confidence ribbons and observed
    outcomes, forest plots of model effects, adjusted survival curves,
    receiver operating characteristic (ROC) curves for one or more
    models, and visual predictive checks of Cox models against observed
    Kaplan-Meier curves. Also provides backwards stepwise model reduction
    by likelihood ratio test.
